.8 lead to 0.0. The engine's choice was H1, and Opus 5.5 took that point next move with no loss."}, {"turn": 33, "text": "The 12k's J5 lost 11.8 points, turning an even game (0.0) into Black -11.8. The engine's choice was C8. Opus 5.5 never gave this lead back."}, {"turn": 34, "text": "After the swings, D8 and C8 were quiet moves that lost 0.0 and -0.1 points. They walled off the left and top, and the score held near Black -11.8 until the endgame."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py parses a pasted board and prints each group's stones and liberty count with a danger flag, and count.py flood-fills empty regions to tally area score and komi for the current position. Neither one generates, scores or ranks candidate moves, and neither looks ahead, so both only inspect the current position.", "stop": false}}